      "heading": "The generic template",
      "html": "<p><strong>Section 1. Who and where:</strong> site or asset name, address, client and contact, your name and qualification, date, start and finish time, report reference.</p><p><strong>Section 2. Scope and method:</strong> what you inspected, what you left out and why, and how (looking, or looking and testing).</p><p><strong>Section 3. Rating key:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Good (G).</strong> No action. Meets the standard.</li><li><strong>Fair (F).</strong> Slight wear. Watch it or plan routine work.</li><li><strong>Poor (P).</strong> A defect. Act within the agreed time.</li><li><strong>Urgent (U).</strong> Immediate risk. Act before it is used again.</li><li><strong>Not applicable (N/A).</strong> Not there, or out of scope.</li></ul><p><strong>Section 4. Findings,</strong> one line each: reference, item or place, rating, what you saw, photo. <strong>Section 5. Actions,</strong> one line each: reference, action, priority, owner, date. <strong>Section 6. Sign-off:</strong> your signature, the date and when the next inspection is due.</p>"
