      "html": "<h3>What should every inspection report template include?</h3><p>The site or asset, the date and time, who inspected, the scope, the method, a rating for each item, findings with photos, actions with a priority and a date, and your sign-off.</p><h3>Should I use a generic template or one for my trade?</h3><p>A generic one is a good start. It holds the parts every report needs. Certificated work needs its own template, because the law says what must be recorded. That includes an EICR schedule, a CP12 and a DVSA walkaround check.</p><h3>Can I send you my own inspection form?</h3><p>Yes. Send it in Word or PDF. Quickler builds the Check from it and every new report comes back in your layout. Your checklist, field names and ratings stay.</p><h3>How should I use condition ratings?</h3><p>A traffic-light scale is common in the UK: Good, Fair, Poor. Some work sets its own. An EICR uses C1, C2, C3 and FI. Whatever you use, explain it in the report.</p>"
